+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository: atomic coupon application
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, now)` that runs one transaction: `UPDATE orders` (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`), `INSERT INTO coupon_redemptions` (`order_id`, `coupon_code`, `discount_cents`, `created_at`), and `UPDATE coupons SET used_count = used_count + 1`, committing on success and rolling back then rethrowing on error. Verify with `npm run build` and a repository test that a mid-transaction failure leaves the order, `coupon_redemptions` and `used_count` unchanged.
+- [x] 1.2 Verify the success path writes exactly one redemption row and each column value (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, normalized `coupon_code`, `created_at = now`) with a repository test against an in-memory `openDb()`.
+
+## 2. Service: ordered rules and discount computation
+
+- [x] 2.1 Give `OrderService` a `CouponRepository` dependency and add `applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` that validates in the exact TASK.md section 6 order (`INVALID_REQUEST`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_INACTIVE`, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`, `COUPON_EXPIRED`, `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED`, `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`) using one `this.clock()` reading. Verify each rejection code and precedence with service tests.
+- [x] 2.2 Normalize the code by trim + upper-case before lookup and persistence, and verify `" save20 "` matches `SAVE20` and that a missing/non-string/blank `couponCode` yields 400 `INVALID_REQUEST`.
+- [x] 2.3 Implement discount computation (FIXED = value; PERCENT = floor(amount * value / 100); optional `maxDiscountCents` cap; hard `MAX_DISCOUNT_CENTS = 10000` ceiling; clamp to `amountCents`) and verify with unit tests for `10000 × 20% = 2000`, `10000 − 1500`, `100000 × 20% uncapped = 20000`, `1000 vs FIXED 3000 = 1000`, and `999 × 15% = 149`.
+
+## 3. Route and wiring
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` parsing the id and passing `body.couponCode` through, returning HTTP 200 with the re-read order. Verify `npm run build`.
+- [x] 3.2 Wire the `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts` and verify the endpoint responds end-to-end through `createApp({ clock })`.
+- [x] 3.3 Add integration tests through `createApp` covering the acceptance criteria: percent/fixed amounts (AC-01, AC-02), clamp to zero (AC-04), floor rounding (AC-05), `amount == minAmountCents` (AC-06), `now == validFrom` accepted and `now == validUntil` expired (AC-07), `usedCount` +1 with one extra redemption row (AC-09), and whitespace code matching (AC-10). Cover the AC-03 scenario (`amountCents = 100000`, PERCENT 20, no `maxDiscountCents`) but assert the REQ-08-capped `discountCents = 10000`; the AC-03 example value of 20000 is the documented conflict and is intentionally not asserted.
+- [x] 3.4 Add integration tests asserting a rejected request (each error code) changes nothing in `orders`, `coupons` and `coupon_redemptions`, and that the success body equals the following `GET /orders/:id` with `status` still `PENDING`.
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build`; it must exit 0 with no type errors.
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm test`; all new tests plus the untouched existing `tests/orders.test.ts` must pass.
+- [x] 4.3 Confirm no schema change, no new dependency, and that existing endpoints/tests were not modified (review `git diff --stat`).
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review, per the OpenSpec workflow.
